    "handoffCoastSec": 0.2,
    "looseScoopFt": 3.5,
    // #609: the S-29 lever since the outfield read went back to the reference. An outfielder on a ball hit in
    // the air runs at the one glove speed x this. S-29 seeds 1-5: 1.18 / 1.48 runs a side at 1.0 with the 0.83 s
    // read, 2.20 / 2.62 at 0.6 (P7's 2.4 s read at 1.0: 2.52 / 2.72). The fly stretch (flight.timeScale 1.1-1.65)
    // and the launch mix moved it under 0.2: the 2.4 s read had been giving away liners, not flies.
    "outfieldAirMul": 0.6,
    // #636: the other half of the lever. Once the infield -> outfield hand-off honours the infielder's route in the air
    // (D17, S-97), an infielder under a ball on the stretched clock (a fly or a pop, flight.timeScale 1.65) runs at the
    // one glove speed x this; on a liner (its own clock, 1.0) an infielder runs the one speed, so the rope SS reaches
    // past the lip is SS's. S-29 seeds 1-5 (main at #642: 2.62 / 2.58): D17 in the air at 1.0 reads 1.92 / 1.76, the
    // infield running back under every short fly past the lip; 0.6 (the real clock) 2.18 / 1.94; 0.5 2.38 / 2.18;
    // 0.45 2.64 / 2.32 and 2.16-2.72 a side over four seed sets with infield pops still caught (0.02-0.04 pop hits a
    // game); 0.4 2.72 / 2.12 and pops start to drop. A flat multiplier on every air ball drops liners in front of the
    // infield instead (hits inside the lip 0.04 -> 0.20 a game at 0.6).
    "infieldAirMul": 0.45,
    // #718 (F693-02-carry-movement-response): the response law. Seconds from rest to the rated speed, and from the rated
    // speed to rest; a reversal is the brake and then the ramp. 0 / 0 is the instant step this table always had; trials/c80
    // carries 0.20 / 0.10.
    "accelSec": 0,
    "brakeSec": 0
  },
